WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.000
I don't recommend
many supplements,

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.300
but a regular, reliable source
of vitamin B12 is critical

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:09.120
for anyone on a
plant-based diet,

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.400
and its deficiency can cause
an array of symptoms.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:16.023
Watch the video to find out
what the optimal B12 dose is.

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:26.169
"The Symptoms of Vitamin B12 Deficiency
and The Optimal Dosage for Adults"

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:32.040
In 1853, a bedridden vegetarian
was reported to experience

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:36.900
a remarkable recovery upon eating
meat. Probably didn't help he was

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.080
an opium addict, but he had
been doing that for a decade.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:44.460
It was only after five years as a
vegetarian did he end up bedridden,

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:46.920
covered in bedsores,
but a little beef

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.900
and mutton and he was
eventually up and about.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:54.840
Can't blame the poor guy, as this was
nearly a century before the discovery and

00:00:54.840 --> 00:01:01.740
identification of vitamin B12, resulting
in just one of six separate Nobel prizes

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.560
awarded for teasing out its
structure and function.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.740
One of the most dramatic events
in the history of medicine

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:13.140
was the curing of pernicious anemia,
a B12 deficiency disease, an otherwise

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:18.120
fatal disorder, with a special diet
centered around calf and beef liver.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:23.100
Vitamin B12 levels start to drop
with months of cutting out meat.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:27.840
Yes, there are all sorts of benefits
of adopting a more plant-based diet,

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:32.100
but underestimating the risk
of developing a B12 deficiency

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.340
nullifies the health benefits
of a vegetarian diet,

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:38.160
or even a diet centered
around plant foods

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:40.620
but contains meat only
a few times a week.

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:45.000
Even moderate amounts of animal
products may not be sufficient

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.840
to restore and maintain
adequate vitamin B12 function.

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:52.380
Vitamin B12 is not made by plants.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:56.520
It's not made by animals either, but
rather microbes that blanket the earth.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:00.600
We presumably used to get B12 drinking
out of a mountain stream or well water,

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:05.220
based on studies showing vegetarians in
developing countries who drink purified

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:10.200
water appear to be at higher risk. But
now we chlorinate the water supply

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:13.440
to kill off any bacteria. So we don't
get a lot of B12 in our water anymore;

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:18.600
we don't get a lot of cholera, eitherâ€”
that's a good thing that we live

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:21.420
in such a nice sanitary modern world.

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:27.600
Vegetarians living in developing world
slums appear to have fewer B12 problems.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:32.460
Basically, the more hygienic
our meals, the less B12 we get.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:39.360
Our fellow great apes like gorillas get all
the B12 they need eating their own feces;

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.760
I prefer supplements.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:45.330
Before getting into the nitty gritty of
how much to take, how frequently,

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:49.500
and which type is best, what are
the symptoms of B12 deficiency?

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:53.280
What aren't the symptoms
of B12 deficiency?

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:56.640
It's known as "The Great Masquerader."

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:00.900
It can cause everything from abdominal
distention and chronic diarrhea,

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:04.320
to shortness of breath and
swollen red painful feet.

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:08.940
It can also cause Parkinson's syndrome-
like symptoms, skin darkening

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:13.920
that resolved with supplementation, and
something I had never heard of before:

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:16.440
bilateral useless hand syndrome.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:21.480
The many faces of B12 deficiency
include neurologic symptoms

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:24.600
such as numbness and tingling in
the hands and feet, muscle cramps,

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:28.920
dizziness, cognitive disturbances,
difficulty walking, erectile dysfunction,

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:32.580
as well as fatigue, and psychiatric
symptoms like depression,

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:38.100
and even psychosis. For example,
a 47-year-old woman with a 5-year

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:41.940
history of psychosis, treated
with antipsychotic drugs,

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:45.960
cognitively impaired,
reporting visual hallucinations,

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:49.620
until finally her mother revealed

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:53.340
that the patient was following
a strict vegan diet for 7 years.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:57.600
She started B12 supplements,
and her symptoms went away.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:03.960
Years of her life lost in a psychotic
haze, all apparently because

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:06.120
she didn't want to take a supplement.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:08.160
But vitamin B12 supplementation

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:12.600
is mandatory for anyone
eating plant-based diets.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:19.500
Becoming psychotic is bad, but hey,
better than falling into a coma,

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:24.360
not to mention suddenly going
blind with multiple organ failure,

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:29.460
all thanks to B12 vitamin
deficiency on a vegetarian diet.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:34.740
Looking into his eyes, they
saw "exuberant haemorrhages."

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:36.960
He was bleeding into his eyes.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:40.200
You don't have to be an
ophthalmologist to recognize

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:46.651
this is not what the back of your
eyes should probably look like.

00:04:47.839 --> 00:04:51.780
Compared to non-vegetarians, those
removing meat from their diets

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:54.960
tend to have healthier body weights,
cholesterol, blood sugars,

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:57.360
blood pressures with
a lower mortality rate

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:01.200
due to ischemic heart disease,
the #1 killer of men and women.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:05.280
However, underestimating the
importance of correct supplementation

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:08.340
of vitamin B12 can
nullify these beneﬁts.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:12.300
Currently, the ofﬁcial position of
associations and governmental agencies

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:17.460
is categorical and unequivocal:
in the case of a vegetarian diet,

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:20.940
even if you eat eggs and dairy,
in fact, I would extend that to

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:24.090
flexitarians eating a few
servings of meat a week —

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:28.440
supplementation of
vitamin B12 is required.

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:31.500
Now, it’s not just
those eating plant-based

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:33.180
that should be concerned
about getting enough B12.

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:36.360
About one in three non-vegetarians
aren’t getting enough

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:40.080
for optimal health and that
may exceed half in women,

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:41.700
especially when they’re pregnant.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:45.840
But this number could run
as high as nearly 9 out of 10

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:47.880
among those eating
strictly plant-based

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:51.060
and 10 out of 10
doing it long-term.

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:56.100
There are three groups of people
who should ensure they have a regular,

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:59.760
reliable source of vitamin B12
by supplementing their diet

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:03.240
with vitamin B12-fortified
foods or B12 supplements:

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:05.400
Those who’ve had bariatric surgery

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.440
(which can sometimes
impair absorption),

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:09.420
those eating plant-based diets,

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:14.100
and the more than a hundred million
Americans older than age 50.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:18.300
Why can’t you get regularly tested
for signs of functional B12 deficiency,

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:21.240
like getting your homocysteine or
methylmalonic acid (MMA) level tested?

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:25.200
Though those are nearly always
elevated in cases of B12 deficiency,

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:29.520
there are rare cases of severe
B12 deficiency manifesting

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:31.200
with normal B12 levels in the blood,

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:35.040
normal MMA levels, and
normal homocysteine.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:36.960
How do we know it was B12 deficiency?

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:41.760
Because within months of B12 treatment
they made a remarkable recovery.

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:46.800
So, best to just take it and
not wait for symptoms to arise.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:50.040
The question is how
much and how often?

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:53.640
Some recommend a single dose
of 50 to 100 micrograms a day

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:55.740
or a thousand micrograms twice a week.

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:58.800
Others suggest 50 to
150 micrograms a day.

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:01.560
Some even recommend
500 micrograms a day.

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:05.580
It all depends on the target
levels you want in your body.

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:09.840
For those with normal absorption
capacity, meaning being under age 50

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:14.520
with an intact gastrointestinal
system and without diseases

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:17.280
like pernicious anemia,
we normally lose about

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:19.680
one microgram of vitamin B12 a day;

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:23.220
so that’s how much we have to
replace, on average, every day.

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:27.600
So, why is the Recommended Daily
Allowance 2.4 micrograms a day?

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:32.040
Well, we only absorb about
half of the tiny doses of the B12

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:35.340
we get in our diet; so, by eating
2.4 we can make sure we absorb

00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:37.560
the one microgram
into our body to replace

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:39.780
the one microgram we’re
losing every day.

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:43.440
Taking larger doses,
like in supplement form,

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:45.840
an even smaller fraction is absorbed.

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:49.020
So, it might take a single
oral dose of 10 micrograms

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:50.760
to get that one microgram absorption.

00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:55.260
But just 10 a day failed to
sufficiently lower homocysteine levels

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:59.520
to under 10 even after a year;
so, maybe we need to absorb

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:03.960
more than that 1.6 micrograms
every day for optimal health.

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:08.700
The current RDA is primarily
based on a 1958 study

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:10.560
that just looked at a
small number of patients

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:12.540
and only measured their blood counts.

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:15.900
Absorbing one microgram a
day may be enough to maintain

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:19.560
blood cell production,
but may not be sufficient

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:21.960
for all the other things
that vitamin B12 does.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:26.160
“Based on the data of several
vitamin B12 status biomarkers studies,

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:29.640
”maybe the recommended intake
for most adults should be raised

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:33.240
to more like four, which is
what you see for example in Europe,

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:35.940
suggesting they want
people to absorb at least

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:37.500
two into their body every day.

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:41.460
In that case you’d need to
take more than 50 a day.

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:45.600
And, now we have data suggesting
getting seven a day may be even better.

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:48.840
So, if you wanted to
absorb 3.5 micrograms,

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:52.920
half of the intake that may
optimize functional B12 status,

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:56.580
how much would you need to
take in a single daily dose?

00:08:56.580 --> 00:09:00.660
This chart isn’t granular enough,
but there’s a formula

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:02.520
you can use to calculate it.

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:05.520
U stands for uptake,
absorption into your body,

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:07.800
and D is your single daily dose.

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:12.780
To absorb 3.5, you’d theoretically
need to take a single daily dose

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:18.780
of about 225, which I round in
my recommendations to 250 a day.

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:21.360
Now, that’s just one of
three methods you can use.

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:24.720
A simpler and cheaper way is
to take a single dose a week.

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:29.220
If you want 3.5 in you a day,
then you’d want to get

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:32.100
at least 24.5 in you in a week.

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:35.400
To get that in a single dose
you’d have to theoretically take

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:39.000
about 2,600 which I round in
my recommendations to 2,500.

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:42.480
OK, but that’s theoretical.
Maybe you need even more?

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:46.740
On the contrary, a new study
showed you can get away with even less.

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:51.900
Just 50 a day (not 250), or
2,000 once a week, (not 2,500)

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:55.140
reliably bought blood levels up,
and more importantly,

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:58.200
normalized methylmalonic acid
and homocysteine levels

00:09:58.200 --> 00:09:59.400
within a matter of months.

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:03.480
So, based on this new study, I dropped
my supplement recommendations

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:08.146
down to that 50 mcg a day or 2000 mcg a week.

